 ["signed-by-someone-absent"]={
  [1]=triplet("Who accepted the fuel delivery?","Fossoil delivered emergency generator fuel; a colleague signed under the scheduled recipient’s name.","The fuel was received and entered into the generator log under the colleague’s own initials.","The docket does not explain why the colleague used the other name.",{"The delivery reached its intended generator and was logged by the person who handled it.","The signature remains a poor shortcut even when the fuel’s custody is clear."},"Fossoil","Fossoil1",
   {kind="dispatch",title="Fuel delivery docket / {CODE}",observation="A triplicate docket with a broad signature over a printed recipient name.",source="FOSSOIL\n{DATE1}\nGenerator fuel delivered to named equipment account. Received under name: {P2}.\nRetained copy and delivery query: {B}.\nDriver note: gate open; recipient requested a quick signature before rain.",note="The docket records generator fuel under {P2}'s name and gives {B} for the retained copy. A generator failure can leave people without light or heat; the signature does not say who held the pen."},
   {kind="notebook",title="Generator fuel log / {CODE}",observation="A fuel log with a fresh total written beside the tank reading.",source="{DATE2}\nFuel received from Fossoil: 180 gallons. Tank sealed.\nAccepted by {P1}; used {P2} line on docket because {P2} was off site.\nGenerator tested 17:10.",note="The log records the fuel and says {P1} signed on {P2}'s line while {P2} was away. It is a custody account, not proof the driver checked it."},
   {kind="receipt",title="Tank inspection / {CODE}",observation="A meter ticket clipped to a fuel-stained envelope.",source="{DATE3}\nTank level matches 180-gallon delivery. Seal intact. Generator run recorded after receipt.\nSignature query closed: fuel accounted for; handwriting not billed separately.",note="The tank inspection confirms the delivery entered the generator supply. The fuel settles where it went, not why the docket used the wrong name."},
